Build a production-quality, self-hosted news-intelligence platform for long-term RSS/news collection, search, analysis, and investigation.

The primary deployment target is Docker Compose. The application must be designed to handle approximately 5 million archived articles without requiring a fundamental rewrite.

Do not casually redesign the architecture below. If you identify a genuine technical problem with one of these decisions, explain it clearly before changing it. Prefer incremental, maintainable implementation over clever abstractions.

# 1. Product goal

The system continuously collects news from configurable RSS feeds, optionally fetches full articles, extracts structured information, archives the data, indexes it for fast search, and provides a rich web dashboard for historical and real-time analysis.

The core application must work entirely without LLMs, cloud AI APIs, or API keys.

AI integrations may be added later as optional plugins, but the core architecture must never depend on them.

Primary use cases:

* archive large numbers of news articles
* full-text search across the archive
* filter by date, source, country, language, entities, keywords, etc.
* identify trends over time
* compare how different sources cover events
* analyze geographic coverage
* inspect entity co-occurrence networks
* identify multiple outlets reporting the same story
* save reusable investigations/searches
* monitor RSS/feed health and processing failures

